{
  "A check box with a label that can be checked, unchecked or indeterminate. It supports an optional three-state cycle, read-only and required states, and validation with its group. It is a native check box styled with design tokens.": "",
  "Checked, unchecked and indeterminate": "",
  "`null` shows the indeterminate dash. Clicking it checks the box. With `threeState`, the user cycles through all three states: unchecked, checked and indeterminate.": "",
  "A box above a list is indeterminate while only some items are checked. Its value is a function of the list, and clicking it checks or unchecks all items.": "",
  "The label appears after the box, or before it with `labelPosition=\"start\"`. With `stretch`, the field takes the full width, so a box after its label moves to the far end, as in a settings list. `labelMode=\"hidden\"` keeps the label for screen readers only.": "",
  "Required check boxes": "",
  "`required` means the box must be checked. It is validated with its group like any other field, and the first unchecked box receives focus.": "",
  "Toggles the check box, using the native key.": "",
  "Moves focus to the check box and toggles it (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "Each check box is one Tab stop.": "",
  "A native `<input type=\"checkbox\">` drawn with `appearance: none`. Its label is a `<label for>`, so clicking the label toggles the box.": "",
  "The native `indeterminate` state, announced as \"mixed\".": "",
  "`aria-invalid=\"true\"`. The text below the label is a polite live region and describes the box.": "",
  "The design system focus ring, shown only during keyboard use.": "",
  "A check box has no strings of its own. The `required` message comes from `uiLocale.strings`, and a message already on screen updates immediately.": "",
  "The field. `data-state` (`checked`, `unchecked`, `mixed`), `data-label-position`, `data-size`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`.": "Field. `data-state` (`checked`, `unchecked`, `mixed`), `data-label-position`, `data-size`, `data-invalid`, `data-readonly`, `data-disabled`, `data-required`.",
  "The layout shared by CheckBox and Switch: the box and its label side by side.": "",
  "The native check box, which is the box itself.": "",
  "The mark drawn over the box.": "Kutunun üzerine çizilen işaret.",
  "The label and the text below it.": "",
  "Unit: the box, with every state (`checked`, `mixed` and `invalid`, each with `-hover`, `-pressed` and `-focus`, plus `disabled` and `checked-disabled`).": "",
  "Units: the check mark, the dash of a mixed box, and a layer over the box (`pressed`, `disabled`).": "Unit'ler: onay işareti, belirsiz kutunun çizgisi ve kutunun üzerindeki katman (`pressed`, `disabled`).",
  "Units: a halo centered on the box (`checked`, `hover`, `focus`, `pressed`) and a ring around the box and label during keyboard use, where the design language includes them.": "",
  "Units: the label (`disabled`) and the row it sits in.": "",
  "The box and its mark, per size.": "Boyuta göre kutu ve işareti.",
  "The space before the label, the distance the box moves when pressed, and what the keyboard ring surrounds (`box` or `item`).": "",
  "`true` is checked, `false` is unchecked, and `null` is indeterminate. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "The label next to the box. Writing `&Name` makes Alt+N toggle it. This is the same property as `text`.": "",
  "Places the label after the box (`end`) or before it (`start`), following the reading direction.": "",
  "`hidden` keeps the label for screen readers only. Every other mode shows it next to the box.": "",
  "A click cycles through unchecked, checked and indeterminate. Without this prop, a click only checks and unchecks, although code can still set `null`.": "",
  "The box can receive focus and is announced, but a click or Space changes nothing.": "",
  "The box must be checked. Adds an indicator after the label, `aria-required` and a `required` rule.": "",
  "Stretches to the full width of its container. With `labelPosition=\"start\"`, the box moves to the far end.": "",
  "The native `<input type=\"checkbox\">`.": "Yerel `<input type=\"checkbox\">`.",
  "Changes the value as a click does (with `threeState`, to the next of the three states).": "",
  "Sets focus on the box.": "",
  "Occurs when the value changes. `e`: `{ value, previousValue, byUser, source, event? }`. `null` stays `null`.": "",
  "`ToggleField`, the base class shared by CheckBox and Switch, provides a label next to a native check box, read-only behavior and the access key. It is exported for use in your own controls.": ""
